{"id":31440,"slug":"the-gospel-according-to-matthew","title":"The Gospel According to Matthew","year":1964,"country":"Italy, France","duration":137,"spine":null,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/31440-the-gospel-according-to-matthew","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/d0cfe3ec5085708fb61a84acff47cf3f/yHqekTzqeCB484N7ZbkrjVrD1FwNqA_large.jpg","description":"A biblical epic that only the Marxist dissident Pier Paolo Pasolini could make, this intensely faithful adaptation of Saint Matthew’s Gospel depicts the life and teachings of Jesus Christ (Enrique Irazoqui, a Spanish economics student and Communist activist), whose unwavering compassion for the poor and defiant condemnation of moral hypocrisy make him a perhaps unexpected embodiment of the director’s own worldview. Stunningly shot amid the timeless landscapes of southern Italy and set to a soundtrack that encompasses everything from Bach to Black spirituals, The Gospel According to Matthew cuts past dogma and straight to the core of Jesus’s radical humanism.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Pier Paolo Pasolini","slug":"pier-paolo-pasolini"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Enrique Irazoqui","role":"Christ","slug":"enrique-irazoqui"},{"actor":"Margherita Caruso","role":"Younger Mary","slug":"margherita-caruso"},{"actor":"Susanna Pasolini","role":"Older Mary","slug":"susanna-pasolini"},{"actor":"Marcello Morante","role":"Joseph","slug":"marcello-morante"},{"actor":"Mario Socrate","role":"John the Baptist","slug":"mario-socrate"},{"actor":"Settimio Di Porto","role":"Peter","slug":"settimio-di-porto"},{"actor":"Alfonso Gatto","role":"Andrew","slug":"alfonso-gatto"},{"actor":"Luigi Barbini","role":"James","slug":"luigi-barbini"},{"actor":"Giacomo Morante","role":"John","slug":"giacomo-morante"},{"actor":"Giorgio Agamben","role":"Philip","slug":"giorgio-agamben"},{"actor":"Guido Cerretani","role":"Bartholomew","slug":"guido-cerretani"},{"actor":"Rosario Migale","role":"Thomas","slug":"rosar